promptTemplate:
Act as an instructional designer applying backward design (Wiggins & McTighe) to a higher-education course.

COURSE:
{{COURSE_TITLE}}

TERMINAL LEARNING OUTCOMES (what students will be able to DO by the end):
{{OUTCOMES}}

COURSE CONSTRAINTS:
{{CONSTRAINTS}}

1. For each outcome, propose one assessment that would provide direct evidence the outcome was met. Prefer authentic tasks over recall-based tests where the outcome supports it.
2. Propose a week-by-week topic sequence (respecting the course length in constraints) that builds toward these assessments in order.
3. Flag any week whose content doesn't clearly feed into one of the assessments above.
